---
// PLATE I — the shipped runtime, one request finding its way through.
// Engineering-drawing emulation of the "I — The runtime — shipped" region of
// plate-full.png (drawing no. LH-ARCH-001). Seven group containers; the numbered
// badges ①–⑦ trace one request along the SOLID accent request path, USER FLOW FIRST:
//   ① you type → ② the channel routes → ③ the agent loop takes the turn →
//   ④ the context window is built and the model completes → ⑤ the loop dispatches
//   tools → ⑥ memory injects recalled context (see Plate II) → ⑦ fenced builtins run.
// DASHED = the pub/sub spine (terminal streams, the loop publishes, tools return an
// observe). All box labels are source-true (see .planning/DRAWING-SPEC VERIFIED FACTS).
// Group hues via @theme tokens (stroke-accent/infra/orch/amber/tool + fill-* + /NN);
// no hardcoded colour. Square corners. Marker ids p1-*. SVG at sm+; FlowLedger rail
// below sm carries the same nine-step story.
import FlowLedger from './FlowLedger.astro';
---

<figure
  role="img"
  aria-label="Plate one of the architecture drawing: the shipped LocalHarness runtime — one request finding its way through, numbered one to seven along the solid request path. One: you type into the terminal channel. Two: the channel routes the request to the orchestrator, which scores an agent card by keyword, Jaccard and capability — live per-turn wiring is still planned. Three: the agent loop takes the turn, running its ReAct cycle of reason, act, observe. Four: the context manager builds a token-budgeted window, compacting at eighty percent, and the model client completes it against a local model server — Ollama, vLLM, llama.cpp or LM Studio. Five: the loop dispatches tool calls to the tool system, where the registry validates them and fires pre and post hooks, running fenced built-ins over MCP and plugins. Six: memory injects recalled context back into the loop each turn — detailed on Plate two. Seven: the fenced built-in tools run and return their result for the loop to observe. Underneath runs a pub/sub spine, drawn dashed: the terminal streams and the loop publishes every step to the typed, append-only event bus; bus-events dot jsonl is the log of record, replayable and resumable. Config loads YAML from org to division to agent."
>
